docs {
  # Get Public Profile

  **Method:** `GET`
  **Endpoint:** `/api/v1/users/{userID}/profile`
  **Auth:** Bearer access token

  ## Description

  Returns current public profile fields only: id, name, avatar_attachment_id and avatar_url. Use this for USER candidate values and USER winners in lucky draws. Name/avatar changes are reflected on the next fetch. Cache by user ID within a page to avoid repeated requests for the same account.

  The caller must be an ACTIVE, non-deleted account. The target must also be ACTIVE and non-deleted; otherwise USER_NOT_FOUND is returned. This route does not expose email, phone, wallet, roles, friend code or Telegram identifiers. It does not create a friendship or grant group access.

  Avatar access rules remain enforced. avatar_url is null if the attachment is missing/deleted/inaccessible; use a placeholder. Response headers include Cache-Control: no-store. A USER option remains an ID in saved draw history even if its account later becomes unavailable.

  ## Request

  Authorization: Bearer <token>. Set profileUserId manually to a positive user ID. No request body.

  ## Response

  **`200 OK`**

  ```json
  {"success":true,"data":{"id":4,"name":"Current display name","avatar_attachment_id":null,"avatar_url":null}}
  ```

  ## Errors

  | HTTP | code | error |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | 400 | `BAD_REQUEST` | `bad request payload or parameters` |
  | 401 | `MISSING_TOKEN` | `authorization token is missing` |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_INVALID` | `authorization token is invalid` |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_EXPIRED` | `authorization token has expired` |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_REVOKED` | `authorization token has been revoked` |
  | 403 | `USER_INACTIVE` | `user account is deactivated` |
  | 404 | `USER_NOT_FOUND` | `user not found` |
  | 500 | `INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR` | `an internal server error occurred` |

  BAD_REQUEST means an invalid target ID. USER_INACTIVE applies to the caller. USER_NOT_FOUND applies to a missing/deleted caller or a missing/deleted/inactive target. Error responses use the same success:false, code and error envelope as the rest of this API.
}
